{
  "_comment": "Institution identity and temporal validity (#718). Keys are institution slugs (estleg:Institution_<slug>). registrikood: the Estonian registry code of the legal person (RKAR/äriregister), taken only from Wikidata P6518 on the slug's identity QID; a renamed body keeps its legal person, so a rename predecessor carries the same code as its successor (registrikood is unique among nodes without validTo). xteeMemberCode: the X-tee member identifier EE/GOV/<registrikood>, emitted only for current (no validTo) institutions whose code appears in the cached public X-tee catalogue data/xtee_members_EE.json; that catalogue lists only members with published subsystems, so an absent code is 'not listed', not 'not a member'. Abbreviation alias nodes (mta, ppa, ttja, harno) carry no identity fields of their own; they are owl:sameAs their canonical node. validFrom/validTo: inclusive xsd:date bounds of the node's identity under this name; open ends are omitted, never guessed. predecessorInstitution/successorInstitution: slugs of the institution(s) this one replaced / was replaced by (renames and mergers). Fields without a public machine-readable source are left absent: the RIK business-register search is not an open API, and the RKAR (state and municipal institution register) codes are not published as open data, so courts, Riigikogu, Vabariigi Valitsus, ministers and generic KOV tokens have no registrikood here.",
